# Crib library generated by eval/build_cribs.py from 69 authentic messages.
# Regenerate with: python3 eval/build_cribs.py --out cribs/wehrmacht.cribs
# One crib per line, tried in file order; '#' starts a comment.
# Columns after the crib are informational: tier, spare letters (length minus
# distinct letters -- what closes the deduction), how the crib was obtained, and
# how many corpus messages contain it.
#
# Tiers 1-3 can reject rotor settings; tier 4 is too short to reject anything
# and can only seed a plugboard climb; tier 5 holds windows of phrases listed
# elsewhere, a hedge against a garbled or differently punctuated parent.
#
# The order is NOT by tier: a tier says what a crib can do if it matches, and
# says nothing about whether it will. Cribs are ordered by evidence that the
# phrase recurs, then by cost, so the ones most likely to end the run come
# first (measured: median time to first hit 10h against 82h ordered by tier).

